Modelica source:
```modelica
connector NeutralPort
  Real e;
  flow Real q;
end NeutralPort;
model Node
  NeutralPort p;
end Node;
model Hub
  NeutralPort left;
  NeutralPort right;
  Node a;
  Node b;
  Node c;
equation
  connect(left,a.p);
  connect(a.p,b.p);
  connect(b.p,right);
end Hub;
model Study
  Hub h;
end Study;
```

Question:
Within the equation scope of model instance Study.h, return the canonical signed member vector for the primitive flow connection set generated there that contains h.left.q.

Target:
h.left.q

Answer format:
Use ascending path:integer entries joined by commas without spaces; coefficients must be primitive, nonzero, and oriented so the first coefficient is positive.
Return exactly {"answer":"..."}.
